    {
      "text": "Poliwrath’s highly developed, brawny muscles never grow fatigued, however much it exercises. It is so tirelessly strong, this Pokémon can swim back and forth across the ocean without effort.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Poliwrath’s highly developed, brawny muscles never grow fatigued, however much it exercises. It is so tirelessly strong, this Pokémon can swim back and forth across the ocean without effort.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Poliwrath in the Alola region are strong swimmers that use the breaststroke. Many children learn to swim by imitating Poliwrath.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its percentage of body fat is nearly zero. Its body is entirely muscle, which makes it heavy and forces its swimming prowess to develop.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s quite a gifted swimmer, even among Water-type Pokémon, but it normally spends its time on land.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "The muscles it has developed through swimming are thick and powerful. When it lands a square punch, it can turn huge boulders to dust.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Swims powerfully using all the muscles in its body. It can even overtake world-class swimmers.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Swims powerfully using all the muscles in its body. It can even overtake world-class swimmers.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is solid muscle. When swimming through cold seas, Poliwrath uses its impressive arms to smash through drift ice and plow forward.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Poliwrath is skilled at both swimming and martial arts. It uses its well-trained arms to dish out powerful punches.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
